    "body": "<h1>Building your first pipeline</h1>
<p>This guide walks through creating a <a href="{{cms:item/1c05e59d-f366-4176-a6ca-8f52ccfb3ce6}}">pipeline</a> end to end: a source connector, a destination connector, and the pipeline that ties them together.</p>

{{ds:component/alert|variant=info|title=Before you start|body_html=<p>You'll need an API key. See <a href="{{cms:item/67e28ef9-df46-446a-9839-8f4bd0b23de1}}">Authentication</a> in Getting Started if you don't have one yet.</p>}}

<h2>1. Create a source connector</h2>
<p>We'll pull orders from Postgres. See <a href="{{cms:item/9abaed7a-d8e0-4359-8beb-09b323107b37}}">Connectors</a> for the full catalog of types.</p>

<h3>Bash</h3>
{{ds:component/code-block|filename=create-source.sh|language=bash|code=curl -X POST https://api.godzilladocs.dev/v2/connectors \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $GODZILLA_API_KEY" \\
  -d '{\"type\":\"postgres\",\"direction\":\"source\",\"config\":{\"connection_string\":\"postgres://...\"}}'}}

<h3>Go</h3>
{{ds:component/code-block|filename=create_connector.go|language=go|code=package main

import (
	"context"
	"log"
	"os"

	"github.com/godzilla-io/godzilla-go/client"
)

func createSourceConnector(ctx context.Context, c *client.Client) (string, error) {
	connector, err := c.Connectors.Create(ctx, &client.CreateConnectorRequest{
		Type:      "postgres",
		Direction: "source",
		Config: map[string]interface{}{
			"connection_string": "postgres://...",
		},
	})
	return connector.ID, err
}}}

